    "body": "Findings (issue-worker-high, before the fix lands). Answers to the four \"To find\" questions:\n\n1. **Where the entry is planned.** The planar ladder (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/levels.rs`, `run_level_walks`) plans the entry arm at two points only: the first pass of the path (`descend`) and pass 0 of each new level (`level_link`). Each other pass start goes through `pass_link` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/ladder_links.rs`. For a centre-cutting tool, `pass_link` always does a rapid and a straight `feed_down` plunge. Only a tool that is not centre-cutting got the helix or ramp there (`restart`, M11.3). Thus the entry is per operation and per level, not per region.\n\n2. **The second piece of the area.** In `hsm_passes` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_hsm.rs`), each piece after the first gets an axial dive spec at `dive_room` with no helix. Its note says \"a separate piece of the area is entered by an axial dive at (x, y)\". That note is informational. It does not say that the dive goes into material.\n\n3. **Offset rings fallback.** Yes, it has the same defect. When the HSM plan falls back to `plan_passes` (offset rings), each ring or piece start that is not the first pass of a level goes through the same `pass_link` plunge. The root cause is `pass_link`, not one strategy.\n\n4. **Why no warning.** `pass_link` plunges with no note for a centre-cutting tool. The only note there is the #1665 case (a pass that starts where the last pass ended). `plunge_law::guard` warns or refuses only for a tool that is not centre-cutting.\n\nPlan of the fix:\n- The pocket family (Pocket, rest 2D, Adaptive) opts in to a new rule in `pass_link`: when the user asked for a helix, ramp or arc entry and the pass start is in material (`plunge_law::into_solid`), the ladder enters it by the asked arm. If the helix does not fit at the start, it ramps along the pass. If the pass is too short to ramp, it plunges and a note names the site, the level Z and the reason.\n- A plunge into a column that is already cleared, or into air, does not change.\n- The rule for tools that are not centre-cutting does not change. No refusal, verify check or post gate changes.\n- Each piece after the first in the HSM plan gets its own entry point from `choose_entry`.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
